\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Up Against Dollar, Strong Versus Basket \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 1997\par 12:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and its fixing basket in brisk trading Thursday amid demand for forints. \par \par \uc2  At 0953 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 194.25 to 194.30 forints, down from 194.64 to 194.69 forints in mid-session trading Wednesday. They quoted the mark at 110.01 to 110.03 forints, from 109.85 to 109.88 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  In some instances, the forint has strengthened to a point just outside the limit of the band, said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a domestic bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  But he said there's no danger of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , because the band has been breached for technical reasons only. \par \par \uc2  Dealers caught short of forints are the reason for the Hungarian unit's strength Thursday, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  'It's pretty active,' he said. 'The bid and asked prices have been really close together Thursday. Nobody's got enough forints.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Wednesday at 194.56 forints, up from 194.34 forints Tuesday. It fixed the mark at 109.92 forints Wednesday, unchanged from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's fixing will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.13% Thursday, up from Wednesday's 20.12%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1002GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9i06ynl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
