\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Dn Vs Dlr, Traders Eye Futures Expiries \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 September 1997\par 12:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weaker against the dollar and steady against the Deutsche mark in thin trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0947 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 197.21 to 197.26 forints, up from 197.03 to 197.08 forints in mid-session trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 108.86 to 108.91 forints, barely changed from 108.81 to 108.86 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'Trading volume has slowed down a lot since last week,' said Peter Luczo, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Inter-Europa Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Luczo said the forint should stay glued to its present spot on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band for the next few days, although he said the forint could weaken next week in advance of the Sept. 19 expiry date of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures contracts on the Budapest Commodities Exchange. \par \par \uc2  The quarterly expiries have in the past caused increased demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by speculators covering their positions, Luczo said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 197.14 forints, up from 196.46 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 108.84 forints Tuesday, compared to 109.02 forints Monday. Wednesday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.14% Wednesday, up from 20.13% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1006GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9a06svf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
