\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Up Vs Basket; No Effect Seen From Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 1997\par 13:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has strengthened versus its fixing basket Thursday and has now returned to its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  The forint has strengthened to 2.25% below the central's bank's midpoint from about 2.20% in mid-session trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Traders had expected the forint to strengthen due to cyclical factors at the beginning of each month and to demand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked by gains in the Hungarian stock market earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'The forint has strengthened since yesterday (Wednesday), but there's no clear direction on the market,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at the Budapest subsidiary of a European bank. \par \par \uc2  The trader added that there was 'no reaction whatsoever' by the market to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement shortly before 1000 GMT that it would cut the interest rate on banks' mandatory reserves Sept. 16. \par \par \uc2  At 1038 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 197.38 to 197.43 forints, down from 197.61 to 197.66 forints in mid-session trading Wednesday. They quoted the mark at 108.57 to 108.62 forints, up from 108.46 to 108.51 forints. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 197.19 forints, down from 197.65 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 108.66 forints Thursday, compared with 108.42 forints Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.13% Thursday, unchanged from Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1105GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9406h3y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
