\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthens Vs Basket In Thin Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1997\par 11:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has regained some of its strength against its fixing basket Wednesday in slow trading. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'We started out at about 2.17% from the midpoint Wednesday and we've slid back to about 2.20%,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Hungarian subsidiary of a major European bank. \par \par \uc2  'Apart from that there's not much buying or selling interest on the market. We're just basically following the dollar-mark trading.' \par \par \uc2  The forint had slipped slightly against the basket in recent days due to usual end-of-month demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Hungarian companies and outflows of money in recent days from the Budapest Stock Exchange, but traders had expected the forint to gradually strengthen. \par \par \uc2  The forint has been steady against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday. At 0949 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 197.61 to 197.66 forints, barely changed from 197.63 to 197.68 forints in mid-session trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 108.46 to 108.51 forints, steady from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 197.69 forints, up from 196.95 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 108.47 forints Tuesday, compared with 108.57 forints Monday. Wednesday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.13% Wednesday, unchanged from Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-09-97 \par \par \uc2  0956GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9306h1j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
