\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Down Vs Basket; Further Weakening Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 1997\par 12:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint weakened slightly against its fixing basket in thin trading Friday, and recent outflows of money from the Hungarian equities markets are seen pushing the forint even lower next week. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading about 15 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  The forint was pushed down several fillers Thursday from its strongest point on the band by usual demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of each month as Hungarian companies pay for their imports. \par \par \uc2  Thursday's weakening has been compounded Friday by further selling interest from foreigners who may be liquidating positions in the Hungarian equities market, said Peter Sipos, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at BNP-Dresdner Bank Hungaria in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  'The market isn't too active Friday,' Sipos said. 'It's absolutely driven by some sentiment on the part of foreigners to sell the forint.' \par \par \uc2  Sipos said it's possible the forint could weaken next week to around 30 to 35 fillers from its strongest point on the band if the current mood continues. \par \par \uc2  At 0959 GMT, just before the end of the regular trading session, dealers quoted the dollar at 195.44 to 195.49 forints, down from 196.83 to 196.88 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 108.73 to 108.76 forints, up from 108.41 to 108.46 forints. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-08-97 \par \par \uc2  1006GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8t06kh1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
