\par\par \b \uc2  FORINT STEADY VS BASKET, COULD EASE AFTER BUX FALL. \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 11 (Reuter) - The Hungarian forint finished steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar/mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket but firmer against the dollar in slack Monday trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian unit finished steady against the dollar at 198.60/65, compared with a midday level of 198.65/70 and an opening of 198.09/13. \par \par \uc2  "It was a slack day with the forint at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resistance level and tracking the dollar/mark," said Attila Behan of ING Bank. \par \par \uc2  Behan said there could be some hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying on Tuesday if the BUX Index of the Budapest Stock Exchange continues Monday's falls which saw it lose 5.82 percent of its value, the second highest daily fall ever. \par \par \uc2  "Some investors may expatriate funds, although we haven't seen any sign of it yet," he said. \par \par \uc2  If such a trend was sizeable it would move the forint substantially below its accustomed level at the resistance level of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats in a 4.5 percent wide range against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made up 30 percent of the dollar and 70 percent of the mark. \par \par \uc2  -- Duncan Shiels, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8b01cz7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
