\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Stronger Against Dollar In Calm Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 1997\par 11:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is stronger against the dollar and weaker versus the Deutsche mark in quiet trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 0944 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 199.66 to 199.71 forints, down from 200.15 to 200.20 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 106.64 to 106.67 forints, up from 106.47 to 106.52 forints. \par \par \uc2  As usual, the forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'It's dead quiet, and we're just following the dollar-mark trading,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a Hungarian bank in Budapest. 'Everybody's only moving (to trade the forint) when they see the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  move.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 200.36 forints, unchanged from Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 106.50 forints Thursday, compared with 106.30 forints Wednesday. Friday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.11% Friday, unchanged from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0955GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8805ux2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40