\par\par \b \uc2  Forint ends steady vs basket,nears 200-mark vs dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Aug 5 (Reuter) - The Hungarian forint finished steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar/mark \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket and brushed against the 200-mark versus the dollar before strengthening by the close, dealers said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The forint finished at 199.67 to the dollar, compared to 199.70/75 at midday and 199.22/27 at the opening. \par \par \uc2  At one point in afternoon trade, the Hungarian unit crossed the 200-mark against a fluctuating dollar but there was no trade at that level and the unit moved back by the close after bottoming out at 199.92/97. \par \par \uc2  "There was an offer or two above 200 but no trades," said Peter Benda of Citibank. \par \par \uc2  Dealers described turnover as calm. \par \par \uc2  "Trade was quiet except when the dollar/mark was jumping up and down," said Sylvia Kucsera of Magyar Kulkereskedelmi Bank. "That provoked some speculation." \par \par \uc2  As its dollar value fluctuated, the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained strong, sticking to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resistance level throughout the day. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats within the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made up 30 percent of the dollar and 70 percent of the mark. \par \par \uc2  -- Duncan Shiels, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8501m8h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\p