\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Stronger Vs Basket, Weaker Vs Dlr And Mark \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Juli 1997\par 12:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has returned to its usual strong position, the bottom of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, in quiet trade Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'The forint is trading close to its strongest point, in other words it is back to normal,' a trader said. \par \par \uc2  The band of 4.5% allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  The forint weakened over the past couple of days as a result of relatively large demand from a domestic and an international bank, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  As reported Monday, another trader said that the weakening was due to rumors of Hungarian companies buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to replace \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated loans with forint-denominated loans. \par \par \uc2  Monday morning, the forint weakened against the dollar and the Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  At 949GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 196.20 to 196.25 forints, up from 196.00 to 196.05 forints in midsession trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 107.28 to 107.31 forints, up from 106.11 to 106.14 forints. \par \par \uc2  Weakening against the mark resulted from the mark's strengthening against the dollar on the international markets, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 196.91 forints, up from 196.04 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 106.79 forints Monday, compared to 106.90 forints Friday. Tuesday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.12% Tuesday, compared to 20.13% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1010GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7t05fca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
