\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Regains Strength Vs Basket In Quiet Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1997\par 11:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--As dealers had predicted last week, the Hungarian forint moved back to its normal strong position against its fixing basket Monday in quiet trading. \par \par \uc2  Around 0930 GMT, the forint was seen trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move 2.25% on either side of its midpoint against its fixing basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  'We closed Friday afternoon at around 2.14% from the midpoint, but the forint moved back to the (strongest point) on the band Monday,' said a dealer at a Hungarian bank in Budapest. 'I think those people who were buying dollars against forints last week aren't really interested in the market now, so the reasons for the forint's weakness aren't here.' \par \par \uc2  As reported, some traders said last week they believed the forint's temporary weakness was due to a slight spillover effect from the Polish zloty, which also weakened against its fixing basket. \par \par \uc2  At 0938 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 192.40 to 192.45 forints, down from 192.52 to 192.57 forints at mid-session Friday. They quoted the mark at 107.26 to 107.29 forints, down from 107.39 to 107.44 forints. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 192.55 forints, down from 192.71 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 107.40 forints Friday, compared to 107.26 forints Thursday. Monday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.12% Monday, compared to 20.13% Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0946GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7l05ayq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
