\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Still Weak Vs Basket, Recovery Seen Next Wk \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 1997\par 12:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint remained slightly weaker than usual against its basket Friday morning, with the weakness seen as a result of the weakening of the Polish and Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The forint is traded as far as 20 to 25 fillers from its strongest point at the bottom of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. Usually the forint trades within five fillers from its strongest point on the band. \par \par \uc2  The band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint, which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  establishes using a fixing basket of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  'Trading is lively with some still spells, which is an effect of the weakening of the Polish zloty and the Czech koruna,' a trader at ING Bank in Budapest said. \par \par \uc2  At 0947 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 192.52 to 192.57 forints, barely changed from 192.49 to 192.54 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 107.39 to 107.44 forints, up from 107.13 to 107.16 forints. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1005GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7i05bya\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
