\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weaker Vs Basket, But Seen Recovering \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 1997\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has stayed slightly weaker than usual against its fixing basket Thursday morning in a replay of Wednesday's trading, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen regaining its strength within the next few days. \par \par \uc2  The forint has traded Thursday as far as 20 points from its strongest point at the bottom of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  That's a relatively unusual deviation for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its normal strong position on the band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'Things are a bit hectic, because there seems to be a lot of movement in dollar-mark trading,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a Hungarian bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Dealers are divided over whether the continuing nervousness that has weakened the Polish zloty has spilled over into the Budapest market, but they said any effect should be minimal and temporary. \par \par \uc2  At 0947 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 192.49 to 192.54 forints, up from 191.94 to 191.99 forints in midsession trading Wednesday. They quoted the mark at 107.13 to 107.16 forints, little changed from 107.11 to 107.13 forints. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Wednesday at 192.09 forints, up from 191.97 forints Tuesday. It fixed the mark at 107.13 forints Wednesday, compared to 107.05 forints Tuesday. Thursday's fixing will be out after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.09% Thursday, up from 20.06% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0957GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7h05csr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
