\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Dn Vs Basket, Small Effect From Zloty Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1997\par 11:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint weakened a touch against its fixing basket in trading early Wednesday, with spillover from continued nervousness over the Polish zloty seen having a slight effect on the forint. \par \par \uc2  At 950 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 191.94 to 191.99 forints, down from 192.06 to 192.11 forints in mid-session trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 107.11 to 107.13 forints, up from 107.02 to 107.05 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint has weakened to about 15 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. Usually the forint trades within five fillers from its strongest point on the band. \par \par \uc2  'There's been a bit of selling the forint against hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said Ervin Csengeri, a dealer at Inter-Europa Bank in Budapest. 'I think dealers are speculating that the decline in the Polish zloty will have some effect on the forint.' \par \par \uc2  But Csengeri said he thinks the forint will return to its normal position at its strongest point on the band soon, perhaps as early as Wednesday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 191.97 forints, up from 191.20 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 107.05 forints Tuesday, compared to 107.19 forints Monday. Wednesday's fixing will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.06% Wednesday, up from 20.03% Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0955GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7g056eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
