\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Steady Vs Basket, Untouched By Zloty Fall \b0\par\par\uc2 235 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1997\par 11:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has stayed rock solid against its fixing basket Tuesday with no spillover effect seen from the weakening Polish zloty, dealers in Budapest said. \par \par \uc2  As usual, the forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  At 933 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 192.06 to 192.11 forints, up from 191.90 to 191.95 forints in mid-session trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 107.02 to 107.05 forints, barely changed from 107.01 to 107.04 forints. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the zloty continued to slide against the dollar Tuesday, with dealers in Warsaw saying they expect a major statement by the National Bank of Poland that contains clues about the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view on the correct trading levels for the zloty. \par \par \uc2  But on the open market in Budapest, trading in the forint is quite sleepy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'There's no effect whatever from the zloty,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a west European bank in Budapest. 'The market here is completely quiet.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0941GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7f057km\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\pic