\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Up Slightly Vs Dlr In Low-Volume Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 1997\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is slightly stronger against the dollar Friday with interest seen muted due to the July 4 holiday in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  At 0925 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 188.11 to 188.16 forints, down a touch from 188.20 to 188.25 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the Deutsche mark at 107.45 to 107.50 forints, up from 107.14 to 107.17 forints. \par \par \uc2  As usual, the forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  uses a fixing basket of 30% dollar and 70% mark to establish the band. \par \par \uc2  'Volume is very, very weak,' said Gabor Butor, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Raiffeisen Unicbank in Budapest. 'The forint's been moving Friday within a very narrow range.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 188.40 forints, up from 187.79 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 107.36 forints Thursday, compared to 107.53 forints Wednesday. Friday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.44% Friday, compared to 20.49% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0940GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7404vbd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal276