\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weaker Against Dollar In Moderate Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 1997\par 14:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in moderate trading at early afternoon Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 1206 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 187.27 to 187.32 forints, up from 185.92 to 185.97 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 107.38 to 107.43 forints, down from 107.71 to 107.74 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading within five fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  As expected, the forint moved back to a stronger point on the band Monday, after spending late last week at roughly 10 fillers from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid due to cyclical factors such as futures expiration and hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  payments for energy imports that weakened demand for the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slightly. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  On the open market Monday, 'the forint has been very stable,' said a dealer at a major European bank in Budapest. He added that as usual the forint has been tracking dollar-mark movements. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 186.97 forints, up from 185.97 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 107.48 forints Monday, compared to 107.72 forints Friday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.62% Monday, compared to 20.68% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 30-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1219GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6u04te4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
