\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Still Weaker Against Basket In Thin Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 1997\par 11:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has stayed Friday morning at a position slightly weaker than normal against its fixing basket in thin trading. \par \par \uc2  The forint has been trading in ranges between eight and 12 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. Usually the forint trades within five fillers of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bases the band on a basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  As reported, cyclical factors such as monthly foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  payments for energy imports were seen driving the forint slightly lower on the band Thursday. \par \par \uc2  'From what we've heard, there's not much activity on the market Friday,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a Hungarian bank in Budapest. 'We expect the forint to go back to its strongest position on the band next week.' \par \par \uc2  At 0917 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 185.92 to 185.97 forints, up from 185.76 to 185.81 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 107.71 to 107.74 forints, up a touch from 107.65 to 107.70 forints. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 185.78 forints, up from 185.23 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 107.68 forints Thursday, compared to 107.61 forints Wednesday. Friday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.68% Friday, down from 20.70% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 27-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0928GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6r04mbt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
