\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Down Vs Basket, Cyclical Factors Blamed \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 1997\par 12:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--Cyclical factors helped push the Hungarian forint to a slightly weaker-than-usual position against its fixing basket Thursday morning, but the forint is seen returning to its usual strong position over the next couple of days. \par \par \uc2  Shortly before 1000 GMT, the forint was trading about eight to 10 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  The forint usually trades within five fillers of its strongest point on the band, which the bank establishes using a basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark. \par \par \uc2  'The forint has probably weakened since we're approaching the end of the month, and there are some payments due (in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) for energy imports,' said Mihaly Donka, dealer at BNP-Dresdner Bank Hungaria in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Donka predicted the forint would return to its strong position on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in the next few days. \par \par \uc2  At 1000 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 185.76 to 185.81 forints, stronger from 185.15 to 185.20 forints in mid-session trading Wednesday. They quoted the mark at 107.65 to 107.70 forints, up slightly from 107.60 to 107.65 forints. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Wednesday at 185.23 forints, down from 185.37 forints Tuesday. It fixed the mark at 107.61 forints Wednesday compared with 107.55 forints Tuesday. Thursday's fixing will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.70% Thursday, down from 20.71% Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1027GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6q04n6z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
