\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strong Vs Basket, Unaffected By Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 1997\par 16:03\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the Hungarian forint was unaffected Tuesday by a rash of news, including a future cut in interest rates, an upgrade for Hungary's sovereign debt and a planned cut in the rate of the forint's monthly devaluation rate. \par \par \uc2  At 1258 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 185.35 to 185.40 forints in late trade, virtually unchanged from 185.34 to 185.39 forints around 920 GMT. They quoted the mark at 107.50 to 107.55 forints, up from 107.36 to 107.41 forints. \par \par \uc2  Throughout Tuesday the forint traded very close to its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The normal trading session ends at 1300 GMT. \par \par \uc2  'The forint preserved its strong position on the band (after the announcement of the cut of the monthly devaluation rate of the forint to 1% from 1.1% as of Aug. 15),' said trader Szabolcs Prisztoka at OTP Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also announced during trading it will cut its base rate to 21.00% from 21.50% effective July 1. That news came shortly after European credit rating agency IBCA said it had upgraded Hungary's sovereign debt to BBB from BBB minus. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1403GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6o04q3e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
