\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weaker Vs Dollar, Steady Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juni 1997\par 11:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and steady against the Deutsche mark in brisk trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 0926 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 185.60 to 185.65 forints, up from 185.39 to 185.43 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 107.36 to 107.41 forints, virtually unchanged from Friday. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  'There's pretty much activity, but there's not any news moving the market,' said a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Budapest subsidiary of a major western European bank. 'The forint's not going to move on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 185.44 forints, down from 185.85 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 107.39 forints Friday, compared to 106.99 forints Thursday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Monday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three-month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.72% Monday, compared to 20.73% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0944GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6n04r7z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
