\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Stronger Vs Dlr, Remains Strong Vs Basket \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1997\par 11:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in quiet trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 949 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 183.54 to 183.59 forints, down from 184.08 to 184.13 forints in mid-session trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 107.18 to 107.23 forints, up from 107.13 to 107.16 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading close to its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  'The forint is trading close to (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) bid and driven solely by the dollar's moves on the international markets,' said Istvan Horvath, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Hypo Bank Hungary in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Horvath added that the forint strengthened against the dollar early Tuesday as the dollar regained some ground in the morning, following the dollar's drop Monday on speculation that France would delay joining the European monetary union. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 184.28 forints, down from 185.23 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 106.95 forints Monday, compared to 106.68 forints Friday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Tuesday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 20.90% Tuesday, compared to 20.93% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP