\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Up Vs Dlr, No Effect Seen From Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1997\par 12:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in calm trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 1052 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 184.08 to 184.13 forints, down from 185.19 to 185.24 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 107.13 to 107.16 forints, up from 106.71 to 106.74 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  No effect was seen Monday on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from the National Bank of Hungary's cut Friday afternoon of its one-month and one-week reverse repo rates, said Jozsef Bodor, chief dealer at WestLB Hungaria in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  'The market wasn't really surprised, and had already priced in the rate cuts,' Bodor said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the one-month reverse repo rate to 20.75% from 21.25% and the one-week reverse repo rate to 20.25% from 20.75%. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1056GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt6904809\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
