\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Steady Vs Basket, Seen Stable Next Week \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 1997\par 11:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has remained strong against its fixing basket in sleepy trading Friday, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen maintaining its resiliency throughout next week as well. \par \par \uc2  At 951 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 185.19 to 185.24 forints, up from 184.49 to 184.54 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 106.71 to 106.74 forints, down a touch from 106.75 to 106.78 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  'The market's not active at all,' said Attila Behan, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ING Bank Hungary in Budapest. 'The forint's just following the dollar-mark movements.' \par \par \uc2  Behan said he expects the forint to remain strong on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in trading next week. The forint strengthened on the band earlier this week following two weeks of relative weakness attributed by traders in part to the turmoil in koruna trading in the neighborhing Czech Republic. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 184.35 forints, down from 184.70 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 106.84 forints Thursday, compared to 106.60 forints Wednesday. Friday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.14% Friday, unchanged from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-06-97 \par \par \uc2  0955GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt66046nw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
