\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Regains Strong Position Against Basket \b0\par\par\uc2 290 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1997\par 12:19\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has muscled its way back to its customary strong position against its fixing basket Wednesday, with the forint seen at last breaking free from the recent shock waves in central Europe caused by volatility in the Czech Republic. \par \par \uc2  Shortly before 1000 GMT dealers saw the forint trading at its strongest point on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a switch from recent weeks in which the forint was seen trading about 30 fillers from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which devalues the forint by 1.1% each month against a basket of 30% dollar and 70% Deutsche mark, sets the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 4.5%, with the forint allowed to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. \par \par \uc2  Zoltan Kalman, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Hypo Bank Hungary Rt. in Budapest, said the forint's rise, which began late Tuesday, is indicative of renewed investor confidence in Hungary, now that it appears the country hasn't been affected by the recent turmoil sparked by speculation against the Czech koruna. \par \par \uc2  But Kalman cautioned against too much exuberance. \par \par \uc2  'If the forint stays strong like this for at least one week, then we can say that the panic is absolutely over,' Kalman said. 'But we should wait a few more days.' \par \par \uc2  At 1011 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 184.67 to 184.72 forints, up from 184.26 to 184.31 forints in mid-session trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 106.57 to 106.62 forints, down from 106.80 to 106.85 forints. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-06-97 \par \par \uc2  1019GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt640420o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
