\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Steady Vs Dollar, Foreign Support Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1997\par 11:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is steady against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in moderate trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 942 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 182.53 to 182.58 forints, virtually unchanged from 182.50 to 182.55 forints in mid-session trading Wednesday. They quoted the mark at 106.95 to 106.98 forints, down from 107.14 to 107.19 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at 25 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The forint has remained at roughly the same spot on the band this week. The forint usually trades near its strongest point, close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid. There are 100 fillers in a forint. \par \par \uc2  'We see no effect (Thursday) of the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's problems on the Hungarian forint market,' said trader Istvan Gere at ING Bank Hungary in Budapest, referring to volatility in Prague in recent days caused by speculation against the Czech koruna. \par \par \uc2  Gere added that such effects were felt in Budapest at the beginning of last week, but 'now it is the opposite (situation) as foreigners are returning to the market.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Wednesday at 182.59 forints, up from 181.73 forints Tuesday. It fixed the mark at 107.18 forints Wednesday, compared to 107.17 forints Tuesday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Thursday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.15% Thursday, unchanged on the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0952GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5t03vrm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
