\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Still Weaker Vs Basket, Czech Spillover Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 1997\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint stayed at a relatively weak position against the dollar and Deutsche mark in early trading Wednesday, with some pressure on the forint seen generated by continuing nervousness over the koruna in the neighboring Czech Republic. \par \par \uc2  'The weakening of the forint is a result of the spillover effect from the Czech market and is not due to fundamental reasons,' said trader Zoltan Toth at Central-European International Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  At 952 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 182.50 to 182.55 forints, up from 181.70 to 181.75 forints in mid-session trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 107.14 to 107.19 forints, up from 107.03 to 107.06 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading 25 to 30 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the midpoint. Usually the forint trades within 5 to 10 fillers from its strongest point on the band. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  Toth said trading in the forint Wednesday is livelier than ususal. \par \par \uc2  Because investors regard the Czech Republic, Poland and Hungary as one bloc, the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also affected by the Czech crisis, although to a lesser extent than the Polish zloty, Toth said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 181.73 forints, up from 180.83 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 107.17 forints Tuesday, compared to 107.27 forints Monday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Wednesday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.15% Wednesday, unchanged on the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0957GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5s03v8q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
