\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Steady Vs Basket After Early Weakening \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 1997\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint weakened mildly against its fixing basket early Monday but has since regained ground and is near Friday's level, in trading thinned by the fact that several banks in Budapest are closed Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 954 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 180.90 to 180.95 forints, down from 181.18 to 181.23 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 107.30 to 107.35 forints, up from 106.96 to 107.01 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading about 20 to 25 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, said Laszlo Egyed, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at West LB Hungaria Rt. in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity, which the bank establishes using a fixing basket made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the forint weakened to around 40 fillers from its strongest point on the band, Egyed said, adding that trading is unusually active given the fact that Monday is a holiday in the U.S. and the U.K. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 26-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0957GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5q03vn5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
