\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Not Affected By Czech Koruna Tumble: Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Mai 1997\par 11:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint has been unruffled Thursday by the Czech koruna's sharp weakening against its fixing basket, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Budapest say. \par \par \uc2  Trading volume in Budapest is merely average or slightly below average, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Although the forint has weakened about 10 to 15 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, that's been caused by volatility in dollar-mark trading, and not by any waves from the Czech market or by increased speculation against the forint, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  'The forint is slightly weaker against the basket, but it's not from the Czech market,' said Attila Behan, senior dealer at ING Bank Hungary Rt. 'It's generated purely from domestic trading and by dollar-mark movements.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  At 940 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 181.35 to 181.40 forints, up from 180.49 to 180.54 forints in mid-session trading Wednesday. They quoted the mark at 106.85 to 106.90 forints, barely changed from 106.84 to 106.89 forints. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 22-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0943GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5m03oe8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
