\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Stronger Vs Basket After Early Wed. Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Mai 1997\par 12:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in lively trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 957 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 180.49 to 180.54 forints, down from 180.77 to 180.82 forints in mid-session trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 106.84 to 106.89 forints, up from 106.71 to 106.76 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint has strengthened against its fixing basket and is trading about five to 10 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, said Janos Toke, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Central-European International Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  'Earlier Wednesday the forint weakened against the basket,' Toke said. 'At one point the maximum spread between the market bid and the national bank's bid was about 25 fillers.' \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  Toke said the forint's weakening started late Tuesday when buying orders for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began to dominate the market. He said the buying orders may have been spurred by Wednesday's deadline for certain exchange transactions, and possibly by investors liquidating some of their positions on the Budapest Stock Exchange. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1005GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5l03n5t\par 