\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthens Vs Dollar, Weakens Vs Mark \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1997\par 11:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in quiet trading Tuesday following the Pentecost holiday Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 945 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 180.77 to 180.82 forints, down from 181.13 to 181.18 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 106.71 to 106.76 forints, up from 106.57 to 106.60 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  'The forint has followed the dollar's drop against the mark in quiet trading,' said \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer Edit Morvai at AEB Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the recent volatility in the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets is affecting trading in Budapest, Morvai said no factors seem to be affecting the market other than the dollar-mark movements. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 181.07 forints, up from 180.56 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 106.61 forints Friday, compared to 106.70 forints Thursday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Tuesday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.15% Tuesday, unchanged on the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0948GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5k03n