\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Dollar In Light Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Mai 1997\par 11:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in light trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 954 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 181.13 to 181.18 forints, up from 180.47 to 180.52 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 106.57 to 106.60 forints, down from 106.76 to 106.79 forints. \par \par \uc2  As usual, the forint is trading Friday at its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, said Peter Piros, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at European Commercial Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  'It hasn't been too active, but we've had some selling interest on the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  side,' said Piros, explaining the resiliency of the forint. \par \par \uc2  The trader also said that the Budapest market hasn't been affected by volatility in Czech koruna trading Thursday and Friday, when the Czech National Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the sliding koruna. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in Budapest will be closed Monday in observance of the Pentecost holiday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 180.56 forints, down from 181.24 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 106.70 forints Thursday, compared to 106.32 forints Wednesday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Friday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.15% Friday, up from 21.14% Thursday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0958GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5g03haj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
