\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthening Against Dollar, Weaker Vs DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 230 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 1997\par 10:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in early trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 846 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 179.50 to 179.55 forints, down from 180.74 to 180.79 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 106.59 to 106.64 forints, up from 106.23 to 106.28 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar-mark trading has been staying in a pretty narrow range, and the forint is just following that,' said Noemi Koppendorfer, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Hungarian Credit Bank in Budapest. 'That's what we expect for Monday.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 180.95 forints, down from 181.54 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 106.21 forints Friday, compared to 105.97 forints Thursday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Monday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates were indicated Friday at 21.14%. Monday's interbank rates will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-05-97 \par \par \uc2  0849GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5c03hbh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
