\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakens Vs Basket, Effect Seen From Rate Cut \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 1997\par 14:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in late trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 1232 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 182.15 to 182.20 forints, up from 180.83 to 180.88 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 105.26 to 105.39 forints, down from 105.40 to 105.45 forints. \par \par \uc2  The forint has fallen Monday by several fillers from its position in recent days near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  'If anything, the weaker forint is because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's repo rate cuts,' said Gabor Butor, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Raiffeisen Unicbank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Saturday it had cut its one-month reverse repo rate to 21.25% from 21.50% and its one-week passive repo rate to 20.75% from 21.00% \par \par \uc2  Butor noted that further weakening of the forint would hinge on whether interest rates on Budapest's interbank money market continue to fall after Monday. \par \par \uc2  One month interbank forint offered rates plummeted Monday to 21.27% from 21.52% Friday, while three month rates fell to 21.21% Monday from 21.28% Friday. \par \par \uc2  But Butor ruled out big moves on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in coming days, saying many market players had anticipated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate cut. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 182.28 forints, up from 180.93 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 105.21 forints Monday, compared to 105.42 forints Friday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 28-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1233GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4s02yav\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
