\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  assets, profit drop in 1996. \b0\par\par\uc2 331 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, April 18 (Reuter) - The balance sheet total of the National Bank of Hungary fell to 5,119.3 billion forints in 1996 from 5,420.4 billion, while its pre-tax profits dropped to 2.46 billion from 6.6 billion in 1995, the NBH said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The NBH said in a statement that its balance sheet total dropped mainly due to the spending of Hungary's privatisation revenues for reducing the country's foreign debt. \par \par \uc2  The NBH's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and gold reserves dropped to $9.7 billion by December 31, 1996, from 12 billion at the end of 1995 as soaring privatisation revenues at end-1995 and early 1996 were parked In the reserve account before being spent on debt repayment, the NBH said. \par \par \uc2  The NBH's net foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt dropped by $4.5 billion in 1996 to $12.87 billion. \par \par \uc2  Relatively high forint interest rates and the creation of convertibility for the forint on January 1 for current account transactions encouraged a drop in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits of banks with the NBH and boosted forint deposits, the NBH said. \par \par \uc2  These foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits fell by 161.2 billion forints in 1996, while the forint deposits rose by 232.3 billion, with forint funds kept in the reverse repo facilities rising substantially, the NBH said. \par \par \uc2  Throughout 1996, the forint was usually pinned to the resistance level of the NBH's 4.5 percent wide floating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range and the NBH increased \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint liquidity by buying substantial amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, the NBH ensured a balanced market by taking up deposits in the reverse repo facilities, thus counteracting the increase in forint liquidity, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  Due to the increase in funds kept in the reverse repo facilities, the NBH's interest expenditures rose by 39 billion forints in 1996, the NBH said. \par \par \uc2  -- Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4i06s8q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
