\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Steady Vs Dlr, Slightly Weaker Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 232 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 April 1997\par 12:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is steady against the dollar and slightly weaker against the Deutsche mark in moderate trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 957 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 180.46 to 180.51 forints, down just a touch from 180.53 to 180.58 forints in afternoon trading Friday following the close of the regular session. \par \par \uc2  Traders quoted the mark at 104.78 to 104.81 forints at 957 GMT, up from 104.69 to 104.74 forints late Friday. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  'Trading activity is average on the market Monday,' said Zoltan Szaloky, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ABN AMRO Bank in Budapest. 'The forint is following the dollar-mark movements.' \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 180.26 forints, up from 179.84 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 104.77 forints Friday, compared to 104.83 forints Thursday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Monday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.26% Monday, down from 21.27% Friday. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1000GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4e02lt0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
