\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint closes steady vs dlr and basket. \b0\par\par\uc2 210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, April 10 (Reuter) - Hungary's forint closed little changed against the dollar in afternoon trade but firmer on the day on Thursday after tracking the movements of the dollar/mark cross throughout trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The forint finished at 179.96/180.06, compared with 179.95/180.00 at midday and 180.20/25 at the opening. Large changes in the dollar/mark and dollar/yen resulted in the forint moving in a very large range of between 179.70 and 180.30 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the international fluctuations scared most traders away from forint deals, leaving no domestic factors to prise the Hungarian unit away from close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resistance level (bid). \par \par \uc2  "The big fluctuations, especially in the morning, made dealers scared about quoting," said Laszlo Egyed of WestLB Hungaria. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats against a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made up 30 percent of the dollar and 70 percent of the mark within the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5 percent wide floating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range. \par \par \uc2  The NBH fixed the forint at 179.84 to one dollar on Thursday, compared with 179.74 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  -- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4a075eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
