\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Down Sharply Vs Dlr, Stronger Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 240 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1997\par 11:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is sharply weaker against the dollar and stronger versus the Deutsche mark Tuesday in trading enlivened by the dollar's muscle-flexing on markets worldwide. \par \par \uc2  At 951 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 179.49 to 179.54 forints, up from 178.18 to 178.23 forints in mid-session trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 104.69 to 104.74 forints, down from 104.95 to 105.00 forints. \par \par \uc2  'As usual, the forint's movements have been driven by the dollar's strengthening on markets elsewhere,' said Mihaly Donka, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at BNP-Dresdner Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Donka said that throughout Tuesday's session the forint has been virtually glued to its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 177.95 forints, up from 176.46 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 105.02 forints Monday, compared to 105.37 forints Friday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Tuesday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.29% Tuesday, compared to 21.30% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 08-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0954GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4802gto\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal276