\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakens Against Dollar, Steady Vs DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 1997\par 10:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and steady versus the Deutsche mark in lackluster trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 834 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 176.31 to 176.36 forints, up from 176.12 to 176.17 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 105.36 to 105.41 forints, barely changed from 105.35 to 105.40 forints. \par \par \uc2  Friday trading has been quiet, with the forint staying near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, said Szilvia Kucsera, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Hungarian Foreign Trade Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band is 4.5%, with the forint allowed to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  'There's no news,' Kucsera said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 176.20 forints, up from 175.96 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 105.39 forints Thursday, compared to 105.30 forints Wednesday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Friday's fixing will be released after 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates were indicated at 21.32% Thursday. Friday's rates will be released after 900 GMT. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0837GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4402hs9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
