\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthening Vs Dollar, Weaker Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 14:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in lively trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 1335 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 176.17 to 176.22 forints, down from 177.46 to 177.51 forints in late trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 104.46 to 104.51 forints, up from 104.06 to 104.11 forints. \par \par \uc2  'The forint market's been relatively active because of the dollar-mark,' said Adam Szilagyi, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ABN AMRO Bank Hungary in Budapest. He was referring to volatility in trading of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday caused in part by news that British elections will be held May 1. \par \par \uc2  Szilagyi said the forint has stayed throughout Monday's session at about 20 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rate. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 176.31 forints, down from 177.45 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 104.52 forints Monday, compared to 104.10 forints Friday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.07% Monday, compared to 21.13% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1340G