\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Dollar, Steady Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 12:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and steady against the Deutsche mark in mild trading activity Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 1058 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 177.46 to 177.51 forints, up from 176.92 to 176.97 forints in late trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 104.06 to 104.11 forints, steady from Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The forint is trading about 25 fillers from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way, said Szilvia Kucsera, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Hungarian Foreign Trade Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Kucsera said the forint opened Friday at about 10 to 15 fillers from the bottom of the band, but weakened slightly during the morning, a normal occurrence on the market. Kucsera also said trading activity Friday has been relatively mild. \par \par \uc2  There are 100 fillers in one forint. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 176.52 forints, down from 177.43 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 104.18 forints Thursday, compared to 103.79 forints Wednesday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Friday's fixing will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.13% Friday, compared to 21.18% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1101GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3e01sn2\par }\