\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthens On News Of Crawling Peg Reduction \b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 12:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--News that the National Bank of Hungary will reduce the monthly crawling peg devaluation rate of the forint to 1.1% from 1.2% effective April 1 has resulted in a strengthening of the forint against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said Monday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the forint opened Monday's session at about 25 to 30 basis points from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, but that at around 1000 GMT the forint began strengthening. \par \par \uc2  'We're seeing hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling as a result of the national bank's announcement,' said Istvan Gere, senior dealer at ING Bank in Budapest. 'It's the foreign sellers that have the large amounts of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell.' \par \par \uc2  At 1109 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 177.35 to 177.40 forints, down from 177.59 to 177.64 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 103.69 to 103.74 forints, up from 103.63 to 103.68 forints Friday. \par \par \uc2  Around 1100 GMT the forint was trading within 10 basis points from the bottom of the band, which allows the forint to move 2.25% from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parity rate. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1113GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3a01p5c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
