\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Dollar, Steady Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1997\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and holding steady against the Deutsche mark in moderate trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 1053 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 177.77 to 177.82 forints, up from 177.20 to 177.25 forints in late trading Wednesday. They quoted the mark at 103.48 to 103.51 forints, barely changed from 103.44 to 103.47 forints. \par \par \uc2  'The level of activity is average,' said Jozsef Bodor, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at West LB Hungaria in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Bodor said the forint is trading about 30 to 35 basis points from its its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Wednesday at 177.23 forints, up from 177.02 forints Tuesday. It fixed the mark at 103.47 forints Wednesday, compared to 103.51 forints Tuesday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Thursday's fixing will be released after 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates were indicated at 21.24% Wednesday. Thursday's rates will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 06-03-97 \par \par \uc2  1057GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt3601lzb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
