\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthening Vs Dollar, Weakening Vs DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 1997\par 12:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in moderately active trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 1118 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 174.01 to 174.06 forints, down from 174.52 to 174.57 forints in late trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 103.76 to 103.80 forints, up from 103.50 to 103.53 forints. \par \par \uc2  'The forint opened Monday about 15 to 20 points inside the national bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band,' said Jozsef Bodor, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at West LB Hungaria in Budapest. 'Since then we've moved to about 30 points inside the band.' \par \par \uc2  Bodor was referring to the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  'There's a lot of selling interest in the forint Monday,' Bodor said, adding that the forint could slide to around 40 or 50 points within the band later this week as market participants readjust their positions in line with customary cyclical trends. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Monday at 173.89 forints, down from 174.55 forints Friday. It fixed the mark at 103.90 forints Monday, compared to 103.54 forints Friday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.45% Monday, unchanged from the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 24-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1122GMT 