\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthening Vs Dollar, Steady Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 1997\par 12:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and steady against the Deutsche mark in active trading Friday. \par \par \uc2  At 1115 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 174.52 to 174.57 forints, down from 174.69 to 174.74 forints in mid-session trading Thursday. They quoted the mark at 103.50 to 103.53 forints, little changed from 103.52 to 103.55 forints. \par \par \uc2  Volatility on the dollar-mark market, as well as increased speculation by Hungarian market participants, pushed the forint up against the dollar about 30 basis points beyond the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5% Thursday, according to Gabriella Endrodi, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Budapest Bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  At the opening Friday the forint was still about 25 basis points outside the band, but that gap has has since narrowed to about 15 points, Endrodi said. She noted there's virtually no risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the forint's moves aren't driven by any change in underlying Hungarian economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  'It looks like the forint will be back inside the band at the start of trading Monday,' Endrodi said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Thursday at 174.75 forints, up from 174.53 forints Wednesday. It fixed the mark at 103.58 forints Thursday, compared to 103.47 forints Wednesday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Friday's fixing will be released shortly. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.45% Friday, compared to 21.46% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 21-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1121GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2l01dtx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
