\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Dollar, Stronger Against DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 243 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 1997\par 13:18\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in normal trading levels Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 1217 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 175.67 to 175.72 forints, up from 174.93 to 174.98 forints in mid-session trading Monday. They quoted the mark at 103.10 to 103.13 forints, down from 103.36 to 103.39 forints. \par \par \uc2  'The market was active at the start this morning, but since then it's dropped off,' said Orsolya Liptai, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at the Hungarian Credit Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  During most of Tuesday the forint has been trading about 20 basis points from its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, Liptai said, adding that the forint's further course would be determined by the dollar's moves against the mark. \par \par \uc2  The band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from the bank's parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 175.64 forints, up from 174.99 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 103.11 forints Tuesday, compared to 103.37 forints Monday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.58% Tuesday, compared to 21.74% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1218GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2i00zdk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\pics