\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Dlr, Market Seen Illiquid \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1997\par 11:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening against the Deutsche mark in slow trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 1045 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 174.93 to 174.98 forints, up from 173.86 to 173.91 forints after the close of the regular trading session Friday. They quoted the mark at 103.36 to 103.39 forints, down from 103.76 to 103.79 forints. \par \par \uc2  At times Monday the forint has traded 60 to 65 basis points from the customary place near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, according to Ervin Csengeri, forint dealer at Inter-Europa Bank Rt. in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band allows the forint to move 2.25% either way from parity. \par \par \uc2  'The market's a bit sluggish, and it's a bit illiquid as well,' Csengeri said, explaining that a temporary lack of demand for the forint has kept the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker than usual in trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  'There seem to be a few more imports than exports in the country, and we've had a small downturn on the stock exchange, with some investors pulling their money out of Hungary,' Csengeri added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 174.37 forints, up from 174.02 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 103.34 forints Friday, compared to 103.25 forints Thursday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Monday's fixing will be released after 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.74% Monday, compared to 21.75% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1050GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2h0100h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
