\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Strengthening Vs Dollar, Weakening Vs DEM \b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 1997\par 11:45\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is strengthening against the dollar and weakening against the Deutsche mark in early trading Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 1035 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 171.14 to 171.19 forints, down from 171.75 to 171.80 forints at the close of regular trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 103.53 to 103.57 forints, up from 103.35 to 103.40 forints at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  As usual, trading in the forint Monday has been closely following moves in the dollar-mark market, said Gabor Butor, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Raiffeisen Unicbank Rt. in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  'The forint has been staying near the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bid, which is the main thing for our market,' Butor said, referring to the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The forint nearly always trades against the dollar and mark near its strongest point on the band. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 171.70 forints, up from 171.09 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 103.40 forints Friday, compared to 103.55 forints Thursday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Monday's fixing will be released after 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.79% Monday, compared to 21.80% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1045GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc