\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Vs Dlr; Market Seen Watching Fed \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 1997\par 11:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and strengthening mildly against the Deutsche mark in subdued trading Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 1041 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 170.39 to 170.44 forints, up from 170.00 to 170.05 forints in mid-session trading Tuesday. They quoted the mark at 103.41 to 103.44 forints, down from 103.52 to 103.55 forints. \par \par \uc2  Lulled by relative calmness in dollar-mark trading elsewhere in Europe, the forint market is also somewhat sleepy Wednesday, according to Zoltan Szaloky, senior dealer at ABN AMRO Bank Magyarorszag in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  'We're still about 10 basis points above the resistance level for the forint, where we've been for the past couple of days,' Szaloky said. \par \par \uc2  Szaloky was referring to the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. The forint nearly always trades near its strongest position on the band. \par \par \uc2  Szaloky noted that the market will be watching for any sign late today from the U.S. Federal Reserve that it might raise interest rates, and that news from the Fed could energize Thursday's trading activity on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Tuesday at 169.95 forints, down from 170.04 forints Monday. It fixed the mark at 103.60 forints Tuesday, compared to 103.47 forints Monday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Wednesday's fixing will be released after 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.84% Wednesday, compared to 21.86% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 05-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1044GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2500v8h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
