\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Forint Weakening Against Dollar In Slow Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 1997\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (AP-Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is weakening against the dollar and is up slightly against the Deutsche mark in lackluster trading Monday on a lack of fresh news. \par \par \uc2  At 1038 GMT, traders quoted the dollar at 169.93 to 169.98 forints, up from 169.66 to 169.71 forints in mid-session trading Friday. They quoted the mark at 103.41 to 103.44 forints, down from 103.56 to 103.61 forints. \par \par \uc2  'There's not too much interest in the forint, because the dollar-mark market has been quiet as well,' said Andras Szekely, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the Hungarian Credit Bank (MHB) in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Szekely said he expects the forint market to stay quiet during the remainder of Monday's session. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the forint is trading near its strongest point on the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band of 4.5%, which allows the forint to move 2.25% either way. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar Friday at 169.70 forints, down from 170.17 forints Thursday. It fixed the mark at 103.61 forints Friday, compared to 103.63 forints Thursday. The fixing basket is made up of 30% dollar and 70% mark. Monday's fixing will be released after 1100 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Three month interbank forint offered rates are indicated at 21.88% Monday, compared to 21.91% at the previous session. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1040GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2300r36\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der S